Third-party components
----------------------

The components below keep their own licenses. Each license text is kept next to
the component in this repository, or is downloaded with it.

- Libertinus fonts 7.051 (lib/project/assets/fonts, docs/shared/_static/data/fonts):
  SIL Open Font License 1.1; see OFL.txt in each folder.
- Noto Serif CJK 2.003 and Noto Serif Devanagari 2.006 (docs/shared/fonts, and the
  web subsets in docs/manual/_static/data/fonts): SIL Open Font License 1.1; see
  OFL-CJK.txt and OFL-Devanagari.txt. The CJK faces are downloaded by
  tools/fetch-fonts.sh and are not kept in the repository.
- MathJax 3.2.2 (docs/shared/_static/data/mathjax): Apache License 2.0; see LICENSE
  in that folder.
- Typeset and Hypher by Bram Stein, and the TeX English hyphenation patterns
  (docs/shared/_static/data/typography): BSD licenses and the patterns' own notice;
  see TYPESET-LICENSE.txt, HYPHER-LICENSE.txt, and hyph-en-us.tex.
- Unicode Character Database 17.0.0 (tools/data, and the tables generated from it in
  lib/core and lib/readers/rst/inline): Unicode License v3; see
  tools/data/LICENSE-UNICODE.txt.
- Pygments 2.19.2 and Sphinx 9.1.0 style definitions (tools/data, and the tables
  generated from them in lib/highlight): BSD 2-Clause License; see
  tools/data/pygments-2.19.2/LICENSE and tools/data/sphinx-9.1.0/LICENSE.rst.
- tree-sitter 0.26.13 and tree-sitter-python 0.25.0 (built by native/tree-sitter,
  linked into guidedog): MIT License; see lib/treesitter/licenses. `guidedog
  --licenses` prints these notices.
- Graphviz 16.1.0 (linked from the system, or built statically by native/graphviz):
  Eclipse Public License 1.0; see the COPYING file of the Graphviz release.
- Typst 0.15.1 and its Rust crates (native/typst_bridge, linked only in builds with
  -define:GUIDEDOG_TYPST_BRIDGE=true): Apache License 2.0 for Typst; the crates it
  depends on, the fonts typst-kit embeds, and OpenSSL (vendored on Linux) keep their
  own licenses, listed in native/typst_bridge/Cargo.lock and the crates' sources.
- libcurl (linked from the system on Unix): curl license.

Test data
---------

Test corpora are used as data only and are not part of the built program:
Docutils sources (tests/data/docutils: public domain, with one BSD 2-Clause file),
the MyST parser's test data (tests/data/myst: MIT License; see LICENSE there), and
the CommonMark specification 0.31.2 (tests/data: CC BY-SA 4.0).
